WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:05.090
While some posters are designed to look flashy
or show off how many A-list actors can fit

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:09.790
into a twenty-seven by forty-one inch sheet
of paper, there are those rare few that aspire

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:11.269
to do something more.

00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:15.940
The following incredible posters are crammed
full of subtext and hidden references that

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.820
you may have never noticed.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.050
Logan

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.939
If there's one thing Logan doesn't — but
secretly does — want you to know, it's that

00:00:22.939 --> 00:00:24.880
it's not your average superhero movie.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.889
It hides this behind a Western-themed poster
that references an era of slow-burn, morally

00:00:29.889 --> 00:00:32.169
weighted films that have long since passed.

00:00:32.169 --> 00:00:37.239
Logan is a story just as much about superhuman
powers as it is the gritty reality of these

00:00:37.239 --> 00:00:41.920
poor characters, which makes the movie that
much more similar to its poster's genre archetype

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.270
than a superhero adventure.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:47.249
It's a poster that's a bit on the nose with
its message — but hides the true extent

00:00:47.249 --> 00:00:50.789
of its meaning until after you've walked out
of the theater.

00:00:50.789 --> 00:00:52.719
As Above So Below

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:57.559
Riffing off its title, the poster for As Above
So Below depicts an upside down Eiffel Tower

00:00:57.559 --> 00:00:59.879
that's pointed in the direction of Hell.

00:00:59.879 --> 00:01:04.820
But what if, in fact, it's not pointing towards
Hell, but is actually representing Hell itself?

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:08.540
Maybe the Eiffel Tower is actually mirrored
to represent the fact that we're all living

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.860
in Hell right now.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:14.000
The image features a tunnel built of human
skulls — using human agony as a building

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.420
block for urban planning.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:19.710
Perhaps the poster is saying that the earth
we inherited and continually corrupt has become

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.290
our own worst nightmare.

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:23.350
Thor: Ragnarok

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:27.940
Of all the films in the Marvel Cinematic Universe,
Thor: Ragnarok has one of the most impressively

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.300
designed posters.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.880
Featuring colors galore, a dope retro-aesthetic,
and some very cool portrayals of the lead

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:37.079
characters, you might be wondering: how can
this thing get any better?

00:01:37.079 --> 00:01:41.539
The answer is simple: a hidden reference to
historic Norse mythology, also known as the

00:01:41.539 --> 00:01:43.770
entire basis for Thor's movies.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:47.909
Those big, colorful rings surrounding the
characters are a direct nod to Norse mythology's

00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:52.890
nine realms and the tree of life, the latter
of which is represented by Thor himself.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:57.060
And in a way, the message the poster is trying
to convey is true — Thor is the central

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:59.820
component in this entire universe.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.200
"Yes!"

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.710
Kong: Skull Island

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:08.420
If you thought making King Kong look as intimidating
as possible was this poster's only merit,

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.420
think again.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:13.910
The design is particularly old-school, calling
back not only to the days of the Vietnam War,

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.440
but also to the movies centered around it.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:20.870
Specifically, Skull Island's poster riffs
on Apocalypse Now, the Vietnam-focused Francis

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:25.660
Ford Coppola classic that featured an extremely
similar aesthetic for its promotional art.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:29.890
From the stylized title font to the helicopters
ripping across a blood-red sunset, Kong is

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:33.880
going one-for-one with its inspiration in
terms of throwback accuracy.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.400
A Cure For Wellness

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.480
If the title alone sends chills down your
spine, the poster for A Cure For Wellness

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:42.780
only serves to reinforce that fear.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:47.260
Anyone who searches for something too good
will invariably end up finding something bad,

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:52.050
the poster warns, displaying a "cure" that's
actually modeled after a Victorian-era poison

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.050
vial.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:57.100
This is representative of the movie's general
theme that, no matter how noble the goal,

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:02.370
trying something evil in the quest for progress
will always result in pain for everyone involved.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.900
The Silence of the Lambs

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:08.240
It's no accident that The Silence of the Lambs
poster is absolutely iconic.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:12.820
This expert piece of subliminal messaging
was crafted to show just how ominous the movie

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:13.820
is.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.040
Why is Clarice's skin so pale?

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.020
To prepare audiences for the abundance of
lifelessness ahead.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:21.230
And that creepy death's-head hawkmoth covering
her mouth?

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:25.400
It's symbolic of the transformation Clarice
must go through to conquer her foes — similar

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:29.560
to the moth in the movie itself, which transforms
within a cocoon that's been stuffed inside

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.450
the mouth of one of Buffalo Bill's victims.

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:35.060
Speaking of those victims, look a little closer
and you'll see that the skull on the moth's

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:37.100
back isn't actually a skull at all.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:41.590
It's actually made of women, a reference to
a famous Salvador Dali photograph, not to

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:46.720
mention foreshadowing of Buffalo Bill's crimes,
and Hannibal Lecter's sophistication and depravity.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:51.680
And that same freaky moth covering her mouth
alludes to — you guessed it — the "silence

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:54.510
of the lamb," also known as Clarice herself.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:55.510
"Yes."

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:56.990
Thanks for watching!

00:03:56.990 --> 00:04:00.480
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:03.010
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

